  "worked_solution": "From the graph, we deduce that the roots are ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=11.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{1+11}{2}=\\frac{12}{2}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=6.$",
